<title>POLAND: Polish yr/yr CPI 16.6 pct in March vs 17.3 Feb.</title>
<headline>Polish yr/yr CPI 16.6 pct in March vs 17.3 Feb.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish consumer prices rose 0.8 percent in March against a 1.1 percent rise in February, bringing year-on-year inflation down to 16.6 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>The CPI index rose 4.9 percent in the first quarter, compared with a 6.6 percent rise in the same period of 1996.  </p>
<p> POLISH CONSUMER PRICES	MARCH    FEBRUARY   MARCH 1996</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)     0.8	 1.1	   1.5</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)	    16.6	17.3	  20.4</p>
<p> services m/m change	    0.8	 1.9	   1.0</p>
<p> services yr/yr change	 20.4	20.7	  20.6</p>
<p> food prices m/m change	 0.3	 0.4	   2.3</p>
<p> food prices yr/yr change    14.1	16.3	  17.8</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
